==============================================================================
PART 4: complement-fold 2x via THM-280 R-relabel  (a,b)->(n+1-b,n+1-a)
==============================================================================
  The REAL fold: T -> T^op realized inside the tiling cube. T^op reverses every
  arc; relabel v->n+1-v restores the base path n->..->1. Net action on free-tile
  bits = position permutation R (a,b)->(n+1-b,n+1-a) WITH a bit flip on each tile.
  Claim: this is an involution on the 2^F tilings, and c3 is invariant => 2x fold.
 n=3: R pos-perm involution:True  fold involution:True  c3(T)==c3(T^op) all tilings:True  fold-fixed-points:0 (0 => clean 2x)
